1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,041
In this lesson, we'll connect Kyntlo
to the other tools your business uses,

2
00:00:05,041 --> 00:00:09,885
like Google, Facebook and Zoom, and add
extra features from the App Marketplace.

3
00:00:10,733 --> 00:00:12,844
Open Settings, then Integrations.

4
00:00:12,844 --> 00:00:15,403
Each card is an account you can connect.

5
00:00:15,403 --> 00:00:18,154
A green Connected label
means it's working.

6
00:00:18,154 --> 00:00:23,015
Bloom's Facebook and Instagram are
already connected, so let's add the rest.

7
00:00:23,015 --> 00:00:26,086
Connections are made once
for the whole account,

8
00:00:26,086 --> 00:00:28,709
so your team doesn't need to repeat them.

9
00:00:29,558 --> 00:00:30,672
Start with Google.

10
00:00:30,672 --> 00:00:34,386
It powers your Google Business
Profile reviews and messages,

11
00:00:34,386 --> 00:00:36,862
plus Google Ads and Analytics reporting.

12
00:00:36,862 --> 00:00:41,814
Click Connect, and choose the Google
account that manages your business listing.

13
00:00:41,814 --> 00:00:44,662
It must be an owner or
manager of the listing,

14
00:00:44,662 --> 00:00:47,695
otherwise your location
won't appear in the list.

15
00:00:48,545 --> 00:00:52,009
Review what Kyntlo will be
able to do, and click Allow.

16
00:00:52,009 --> 00:00:56,607
Then choose the business location to
connect, and click Connect location.

17
00:00:56,607 --> 00:00:58,560
That's it: Google is connected.

18
00:00:59,413 --> 00:01:02,488
If you hold online
consultations, connect Zoom.

19
00:01:02,488 --> 00:01:06,218
Then, when you set a calendar's
meeting location to Zoom,

20
00:01:06,218 --> 00:01:09,751
every booking gets its own
meeting link automatically,

21
00:01:09,751 --> 00:01:12,238
in the confirmation and the reminders.

22
00:01:13,087 --> 00:01:18,329
To change what's connected, for example to
add another Facebook page, click Manage.

23
00:01:18,329 --> 00:01:21,866
And if you ever need to remove
access, click Disconnect.

24
00:01:21,866 --> 00:01:24,076
Kyntlo stops syncing straight away.

25
00:01:24,076 --> 00:01:28,371
If a connection ever stops working,
usually after a password change,

26
00:01:28,371 --> 00:01:30,202
disconnect and connect again.

27
00:01:31,053 --> 00:01:32,362
What about payments?

28
00:01:32,362 --> 00:01:35,504
Stripe is connected from
Payments, Integrations,

29
00:01:35,504 --> 00:01:38,319
so it sits with your
invoices and products.

30
00:01:38,319 --> 00:01:40,872
We set it up step by step in Module 12,

31
00:01:40,872 --> 00:01:45,520
including how to take deposits
automatically when patients book online.

32
00:01:46,369 --> 00:01:49,636
For everything else,
there's the App Marketplace.

33
00:01:49,636 --> 00:01:54,103
Click Open App Marketplace, or App
Marketplace in the main sidebar.

34
00:01:54,103 --> 00:01:59,370
Apps add extra features to Kyntlo, from
accounting and e-commerce to team chat.

35
00:01:59,370 --> 00:02:01,436
Browse by category on the left.

36
00:02:02,287 --> 00:02:04,960
Bloom's team wants
new-lead alerts in Slack.

37
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:07,146
Search for Slack, and click Install.

38
00:02:07,146 --> 00:02:11,459
Read what the app will be able to
access, then click Allow and Install.

39
00:02:11,459 --> 00:02:15,651
Only install apps you trust, because
they can read your account data.

40
00:02:15,651 --> 00:02:18,323
Most apps then have
their own settings page,

41
00:02:18,323 --> 00:02:22,272
where you choose things like which
Slack channel gets the alerts.

42
00:02:23,121 --> 00:02:26,871
The Installed Apps tab lists
everything added to this account,

43
00:02:26,871 --> 00:02:31,711
so you can review your apps from time to
time, and remove any you no longer use.

44
00:02:31,711 --> 00:02:36,126
Some apps charge their own fee, which
is always shown before you install.

45
00:02:36,978 --> 00:02:38,032
Here's a pro tip.

46
00:02:38,032 --> 00:02:42,747
Before paying for a connector like
Zapier, check what Kyntlo can already do.

47
00:02:42,747 --> 00:02:46,592
Workflows can send webhooks and
update Google Sheets directly,

48
00:02:46,592 --> 00:02:49,631
which often covers it for
a fraction of the cost.

49
00:02:50,501 --> 00:02:51,932
Your tools are connected!

50
00:02:51,932 --> 00:02:56,682
Next, we'll look at billing: your wallet,
your usage, and how wholesale rates work.

51
00:02:56,682 --> 00:02:57,483
See you there.
